{
  "summary": "Updates `-acceptnonstdtxn=1` on test networks so that mempool policy checks only enforce potential consensus script flags rather than standard non-mandatory script verify flags. It replaces a heuristic flag-mask test in `CheckInputScripts` with an explicit enum designating whether a check is for a block or a mempool acceptance, and introduces compile-time validation to verify that consensus script flags are always covered by standard script verify flags.",
  "problem": "On test networks, configuring `-acceptnonstdtxn=1` allowed non-standard transaction structures into the mempool, but policy script verification still unconditionally enforced `STANDARD_SCRIPT_VERIFY_FLAGS`. Developers testing future soft forks or experimental transactions using opcodes like `OP_SUCCESS` or `OP_NOPx` were unable to relay or test transactions in mempools without mining them directly into blocks.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author PR description: 'This PR changes -acceptnonstdtxn=1 so that it also skips the non-mandatory script checks, allowing txs that (eg) use OP_NOPx or OP_SUCCESS into the mempool. This remains only available on test nets.'",
    "Commit 54b11fe9c9 updates MemPoolAccept to use chainstate consensus script flags instead of STANDARD_SCRIPT_VERIFY_FLAGS when require_standard is disabled."
  ],
